#: ../../../system/arm/nuvoton.rst:128
msgid ""
"Some pre-built OpenBMC images for QEMU Nuvoton machines may be available on "
"Jenkins:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/arm/nuvoton.rst:131
msgid "https://jenkins.openbmc.org/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/arm/nuvoton.rst:133
msgid ""
"To find a pre-built MTD image on Jenkins, start from the Jenkins home page "
"and open the ``latest-master`` job. Select the matrix configuration whose "
"``target`` matches the OpenBMC machine name, for example ``label=docker-"
"builder,target=gbs``, then open its latest successful build's artifacts. The "
"MTD image is usually published under ``openbmc/build/tmp/deploy/images/"
"<machine>/`` as ``obmc-phosphor-image-<machine>-<timestamp>.static.mtd``. If "
"Jenkins does not list a matching target, or the build artifacts do not "
"include an MTD image, there is no current pre-built MTD image for that "
"machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/arm/nuvoton.rst:143
msgid "The firmware image should be attached as an MTD drive. Example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/arm/nuvoton.rst:145
msgid ""
"$ qemu-system-arm -machine quanta-gbs-bmc -nographic \\\n"
"    -drive file=obmc-phosphor-image-gbs-xxxxxx.static.mtd,if=mtd,bus=0,"
"unit=0,format=raw"
msgstr ""

